/**
 * Where an individual site is drawn.
 *
 * The register holds a district and a taluk for every site and no coordinate,
 * so a pin cannot be placed at the site itself. What it can be placed at,
 * truthfully, is somewhere inside the right taluk — these are points sampled
 * within each taluk's real boundary, spaced apart so pins do not hide one
 * another, and fixed by a seed so a site does not move between page loads or
 * between two people's screens in the same meeting.
 *
 * So the position of a pin within a taluk carries no meaning and the screen
 * says so. Which taluk it is in does, and that is the part the register can
 * actually support. When sites are registered with a village — as the field
 * app captures them — the village centroid replaces the slot and the caveat
 * goes with it.
 */
